    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "The business impact of excessive operational overhead is substantial but often hidden. Engineering velocity slows as more time goes to keeping existing systems running rather than building new capabilities. Mean time to recovery increases because complex systems are harder to debug. Hiring becomes harder because managing operational complexity isn't attractive to many engineers. Most insidiously, high operational overhead creates organizational calcification-teams become unwilling to make necessary architectural changes because the migration complexity seems insurmountable, locking the organization into increasingly outdated technical foundations."
